+// RewindBox (patch 0038): the mapped region (MapPhysicalMemory's alias region, where the game's NVN memory pools and the GPU's per-frame zero-copy buffers live) kept anonymous
+//   inside the file-backed window, so that only the game heap is in the files. IPA 750 (iPhone17,2, 7,619 MB of RAM, Mario Kart World, window in 1 GB files): on average
+//   401 MB read back from the files and 27,886 page-ins per 10 s (peak 821 MB), in step with the stutters; at the session's end 1,171 MB of the alias region was mapped.
+//   S2Arm measured the same: nearly all file writes come from this region, mostly pages the game had already released (Duo: 9.4 GB written uncarved, 33 MB carved).
+//   The cost is this region's resident pages counted in the footprint. Ported (MIT) from S2Arm c1d9fd9c, d8b0f8fd, 0b2d2d26, 07314902 and f83bd54a, adapted to the
+//   window files of patch 0036: the fallback mapping back to the files goes one file at a time (gf_at), as s2a_guest_zero does; a session reset gives the region back
+static int g_low_tier;           // this session's device cannot hold the pool and the host estimate in physical memory, and the previous session did not die: carve.
